EXT. GLACIER - CREVASSE LIP - DAY

Wind. Blue ice. Two climbers roped together on a slope that ends in air.

LEILANI KEAWE, 30s, hauling on a rope, braced against an axe. CORMAC BRANNIGAN, 40s, dangling thirty feet below in a harness, face white.

LEILANI
(shouting down)
Hold on!

CORMAC
(shouting up)
I'm holding!

LEILANI
(to both of them)
Come on, come on, come on.

The rope creaks. Ice crumbles. She grunts. Digs in.

LEILANI (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Don't look down. Don't look down.

CORMAC
Leilani! My leg!

LEILANI
What about it?

CORMAC
It's gone numb!

LEILANI
(to the ice)
Of course it is.

She heaves. He rises a foot. The axe slips. She jams it deeper.

LEILANI (CONT'D)
(to Cormac)
Kick the wall! Find a hold!

CORMAC
I can't feel anything!

LEILANI
(to the sky)
Please.

Cormac swings. Boots scrape ice. A foothold. He steadies.

CORMAC
I've got something!

LEILANI
Then climb!
